# Do not deploy to production until the user tests

The user asked: after each change, let them test first. Do not push `main` or `vercel deploy --prod` unless they explicitly say to ship / go live.

## How

This repo is linked to Vercel project `usegrokbot` (team `aipost`). GitHub `a70win-wq/usegrokbot` is connected; `main` is the production branch.

Preferred: commit on the current working branch (not `main`) and `git push -u origin HEAD`. That creates a Vercel **preview**. Give the user the preview URL so they can test.

If they later say to ship:

```bash
git push origin HEAD:main
```

or, if git is unavailable:

```bash
vercel deploy --prod -y --no-wait --scope aipost
vercel inspect <deployment-url>
```

Then give https://usegrokbot.com and the deployment URL.

## Do not

- Push `main` or production-deploy as part of finishing a normal UI/copy change
- Change Vercel env vars, domains, or project settings as part of a normal deploy
- Skip the preview URL. They need something to test.
